---
description: Org-wide Node.js Express conventions for EF services
globs: src/**/*
alwaysApply: true
---

# Tech Stack

- Node.js >= 18, Express 4.x
- Plain JavaScript, CommonJS (`require` / `module.exports`) — do not introduce TypeScript
- Entry: `src/index.js`; app factory: `src/libs/app.js`

# Project Layout

- `src/routes/` — `express.Router()`, `*.route.js`
- `src/controllers/` — HTTP handlers, `*.controller.js`
- `src/services/` — business logic and integrations, `*.service.js`
- `src/models/` — domain POJOs, `*.model.js`
- `src/middlewares/` — request/error middleware
- `src/config/` — env validation (Joi), logger, vault
- `src/libs/` — app bootstrap, redis client setup
- `src/components/` — in-memory singletons (e.g. datastructure.manager.js)
- `tests/` — mirrors `src/` layout

# API Patterns

- Layered: routes → controllers → services → models
- Controllers: async handlers, `res.status().json()`, structured Winston logs
- Logging metadata: `{ className, methodName, CID }` using `req.correlationId`
- Errors: throw `ApiError`; `errorConverter` + `errorHandler` middleware normalize responses
- Validation: Joi for env vars in `src/config/config.js` — not ad-hoc in routes

# Middleware

- `requestInterceptor` — correlation ID (`correlationId` header), tenant from FQDN or `tenantid` header
- Attach `req.correlationId` and `req.tenantId` before controller logic

# Code Style

- ESLint: airbnb-base + jest + security + prettier
- Prettier: `printWidth: 150`, `trailingComma: "none"`
- `no-console: error` — use Winston logger
- File naming: `agent.route.js`, `agent.controller.js`, `agent.service.js`

# EF Libraries

- `ef-keycloak-connect`, `ef-stompit` — use existing wrappers, do not replace
- Multi-tenant bootstrap via CX Tenant service in `src/index.js`

# Do Not

- Do not add TypeScript, NestJS, or ES module `import` syntax
- Do not bypass layered architecture (business logic in routes)
- Do not hardcode credentials — use env + Vault
